from pathlib import Path
import json
H=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;O=H/'augmentation';r=json.loads((O/'evaluation.json').read_text())
names={'residual_budget':'Matched residual','mhc':'mHC','single_pass':'Single-Pass mHC','tree897':'Incumbent tree recipe','tree1217':'Unsubmitted v15 tree recipe'}
lines=['# Synthetic data utility trial','','Both arms contain 4,680 training rows and identical class counts. Synthetic treatment replaces 471 resampled-real rows with the three history views of 157 generated pairs. Original examples, scaling and optimization are otherwise fixed. The neural endpoints use three fixed seeds; tree endpoints use the established fixed recipe.','','| Endpoint | Mean log-loss improvement | Mean Pair AP change | Mean sparse AP change | Data gate passed |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for v,d in r['decisions'].items():
    m=d['mean_deltas'];lines.append(f"| {names[v]} | {m['logloss_improvement']:+.6f} | {m['pair_ap']:+.6f} | {m['sparse_ap']:+.6f} | {d['passed_data_screen']} |")
lines+=['','Positive log-loss improvement means lower loss with synthetic data. These are synthetic-versus-matched-resampling differences, not leaderboard gains. All outcomes are retained.','','## Limits and decision','','The neural data gate requires mean paired loss improvement ≥ .001, mean Pair AP change ≥ 0, and worst history-mean Pair AP change ≥ −.001. The tree data gate requires mean weighted pair/behavior change ≥ .0001, worst ≥ −.003, and mean sparse AP change ≥ 0. Passing one endpoint is exploratory, because several endpoints share reused development pools.','','The tested generator passed legal and coarse hand-level checks but failed a deeper benign-pair source check (AUC .9879) and lacked active tilt controls. Therefore this version is not ready for 10× expansion regardless of a favorable small-screen result. A separately generated stack/attendance/tilt repair was prepared using training-only diagnostics; it was not substituted into this trial.','','Any larger trial requires realistic ordinary histories, independent policy/behavior coverage, a frozen new recipe and the existing robustness gates. The known and omitted-family mHC experiment is separate. No production candidate or submission follows directly from this report.','','See [complete results](augmentation/evaluation.json), [frozen trial plan](augmentation/plan.json), and [generator provenance](README.md).','']
(H/'RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf-8')
print(json.dumps({v:d['passed_data_screen'] for v,d in r['decisions'].items()}))
